# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
from fams import *
F = 'igverify'
page('instagram-video-selfie-rejected-again', F, 'Instagram Video Selfie Rejected Again: What to Check',
 'Instagram keeps rejecting your video selfie? The usual reasons, from lighting to face angles, and how to record one that reads clearly.',
 'Instagram video selfie rejected again?', 'Video selfie rejected',
 'A rejected selfie is usually a quality problem, not a verdict on you. These are the things to fix.',
 'Instagram rejects video selfies that are dark, blurry, cropped, or recorded with a filter, a mask or something covering the face. Record in daylight or a bright room, hold the phone at eye level, remove filters and follow every on-screen movement slowly. If it fails again, do not keep submitting. Check the likely cause first.',
 [('Light on your face', 'Face a window or a lamp. Avoid backlight from behind you.'),
  ('Nothing on the face', 'No filters, masks, heavy shadows or hands in front.'),
  ('Follow the prompts slowly', 'Turn your head when asked, at a steady pace.')],
 [S('Frequent causes', ul(['Poor light, or a bright window behind you.', 'A cover over the front camera, a cracked lens or a blurred lens.', 'The phone held too low or too far away.', 'Moving too much, so the system cannot read the face.']),
    'A second person holding nothing, no one else in the frame, and a plain background help.'),
  S('How to retry', ol(['Clean the front camera and sit in a bright room.', 'Hold the phone at eye level and keep your whole face in the frame.', 'Follow each movement slowly and wait for the prompt to change.', 'Submit once, then wait for the answer instead of repeating.']),
    'If you have tried several times, tell us what the rejection message says.')],
 [('Does a rejected selfie mean the appeal failed?', 'Not necessarily. It may only mean the video was unreadable. Look for the message that follows.'),
  ('Can I use a photo instead?', 'Only if the flow offers it. Do not upload edited or old photos.'),
  ('Can Unbanz record the selfie for me?', 'No. The selfie must be of you. We help you understand the request.')],
 ['People rejected after several attempts.', 'Owners in dim rooms or with an older phone.', 'Anyone whose selfie screen stops at checking.'])

page('instagram-selfie-verification-keeps-looping', F, 'Instagram Selfie Verification Keeps Looping',
 'Instagram asks for a selfie again right after you sent one? Why verification loops, which causes are common and what to change before another try.',
 'Instagram selfie verification keeps repeating?', 'Selfie verification loop',
 'If it asks again and again, something in the flow is not completing. These are the likely points.',
 'A selfie loop usually means the upload never completed, the app has a stale session, or the video was not readable. Close and update the app, switch to a steady connection, and finish the whole flow without leaving the screen. If it repeats, note at which step it returns, and send us the screens.',
 [('Stay on the screen', 'Leaving the app during upload can cancel it.'),
  ('Use a steady connection', 'Wi-Fi is better than weak mobile data.'),
  ('Update the app', 'Old versions often break verification.')],
 [S('Why it repeats', ul(['The upload stalled on a weak connection.', 'The app was closed or backgrounded in the middle.', 'The video failed the quality check and the next screen is the same request.', 'The account state changed during the flow.'])),
  S('Fixes to try', ol(['Update the app and restart the phone.', 'Switch to Wi-Fi and disable any VPN.', 'Complete the selfie in one go, without switching apps.', 'If it loops again, record the screen and send us a short description.']))],
 [('Should I keep retrying?', 'A few careful tries is fine. Many rapid ones can trigger more holds.'),
  ('Does the loop mean I was rejected?', 'No. Rejections show a message. A loop is usually a technical problem.'),
  ('Does it matter which device I use?', 'Yes. A device you have used before often works better.')],
 ['People who finish and are asked again.', 'Users on slow connections.', 'Anyone whose app shows a spinner and resets.'])

page('instagram-id-request-accepted-documents', F, 'Instagram ID Request: Which Documents Are Accepted',
 'Instagram asked for ID and you do not know which document to send? The usual document types, what has to be visible and what to avoid uploading.',
 'Instagram asked for ID: what can you upload?', 'Accepted ID documents',
 'Instagram wants a document that shows your name and, sometimes, your date of birth. Here is what usually works.',
 'Instagram asks for a government-issued document with your name, and often a date of birth and photo. Typical choices are a passport, a national ID card or a driving licence. Upload a clear, uncropped photo of the original. Do not send edited scans, photos of screens, or documents that belong to someone else.',
 [('Original, not a copy', 'A photo of the real document is better than a screenshot or photocopy.'),
  ('Everything readable', 'All four corners visible and the text sharp.'),
  ('Matching details', 'The name should match the one on the account when possible.')],
 [S('What usually works', ul(['A passport photo page.', 'A national ID card, front and back where asked.', 'A driving licence.', 'Other documents named on the request screen for your country.']),
    'The request screen lists what is accepted for you. Follow that list over any general advice.'),
  S('What to avoid', ul(['Blurry or cropped photos, or photos of a screen.', 'Documents that are expired, if the screen says valid only.', 'Someone else’s document, even a family member’s.', 'Edited or covered details, other than what the screen says to hide.']),
    'Your document goes to Instagram through the official screen. We never need a copy of it.')],
 [('Do I have to send ID?', 'Only if the request asks for it. If it does, follow the steps on the official screen.'),
  ('Is it safe to upload?', 'Only through the official Instagram screen. Never send it to a third party in a message.'),
  ('Will Unbanz ask for my ID?', 'No. Upload it only on the official screen.')],
 ['People who got an ID request on a disabled account.', 'Anyone unsure what to upload.', 'Owners whose upload keeps failing.'])

page('instagram-id-name-does-not-match-profile', F, 'Instagram ID Name Does Not Match Your Profile',
 'Your ID shows a different name from your Instagram profile and the verification fails? Why this is common, what to explain and how to prepare.',
 'ID name does not match your Instagram profile?', 'ID name mismatch',
 'Profiles use nicknames, brand names and married names. Instagram knows that, but it helps to explain.',
 'It is common for a profile name to differ from the name on an ID, such as a nickname, a stage name, a business name or a changed surname. If the request lets you add an explanation, say plainly how the two connect. If not, upload the document, keep other details consistent and send only what the screen asks.',
 [('Explain the link', 'A single sentence like stage name for the same person is enough.'),
  ('Keep other details consistent', 'Same date of birth and country across the account and ID.'),
  ('Do not edit the profile', 'Changing the name mid-process can raise more flags.')],
 [S('Why it happens', ul(['A nickname or shortened name on the profile.', 'A married or changed surname.', 'A business or brand name used instead of a personal name.', 'A different alphabet or transliteration.']),
    'A reviewer is looking for whether you are the person behind the account, not for an exact match.'),
  S('How to prepare', ol(['Compare your ID and your profile name and note the difference.', 'If there is a text box, write one or two sentences about the connection.', 'Upload a clean, complete photo of the document.', 'Keep a screenshot of the request and the date.']))],
 [('Will a mismatch always fail?', 'No. It makes the request harder, but it is not the end of it.'),
  ('Should I change my profile name first?', 'No. Changing it mid-process can look like a new problem.'),
  ('Can I use a different document?', 'If a second document shows the name used on the profile, it can help. Follow the official screen.')],
 ['People who use a stage or business name.', 'Owners who changed their surname.', 'Anyone with a transliterated name.'])

page('instagram-id-request-no-photo-id', F, 'Instagram Asks for ID and You Do Not Have One',
 'Instagram asked for photo ID and you cannot provide it, for age or other reasons? Alternatives to check on the screen and what to explain in the request.',
 'Instagram asks for ID and you have none?', 'No photo ID available',
 'Not everyone has a passport or a licence, especially younger people. There may still be a way through.',
 'If you have no photo ID, read the request screen closely, because it often lists other documents or a different method such as a video selfie. Do not borrow someone else’s ID. If nothing fits, explain your situation in the request and tell us what the screen offers. Some situations have no route.',
 [('Read the options', 'The screen may list other documents or a selfie.'),
  ('Never use another person’s', 'Even a parent’s ID can lead to a refusal.'),
  ('Explain in words', 'If a text box exists, say why you do not have the document.')],
 [S('Who commonly lacks ID', ul(['Teens and young adults without a passport or licence.', 'People whose ID is being renewed.', 'People in places where ID cards are not common.', 'People who lost their documents.']),
    'The age rule is separate. Instagram’s minimum age still applies to everyone.'),
  S('What to try', ol(['Read each option on the request screen and choose the one that matches your situation.', 'Use the video selfie method if it is offered.', 'If you are waiting on a replacement document, mention that in the explanation.', 'Send us the screen if you are unsure.']),
    'We will not ask you for a document, and we will not suggest forging or borrowing one.')],
 [('Can a school card or a bank card work?', 'Only if the request screen lists it. Otherwise it will not be accepted.'),
  ('What if I am under the minimum age?', 'Instagram’s age rule applies, and an appeal will not change it.'),
  ('Is a video selfie enough?', 'Sometimes. Use it when the screen offers it.')],
 ['People without a passport or licence.', 'Anyone whose ID was lost or is being renewed.', 'Owners who see only an upload option.'])

page('instagram-confirm-you-are-human-loop', F, 'Instagram Confirm You Are Human Loop: What to Try',
 'Instagram keeps asking you to confirm you are human and never lets you in? Why this check repeats and what to change on your phone and network.',
 'Instagram keeps asking you to confirm you are human?', 'Confirm you are human loop',
 'This check appears when behavior or a network looks automated. Looping means it is not passing.',
 'The human check appears when Instagram sees activity that looks automated, or a login from a network that many accounts share. Looping usually means the check cannot complete, because of a VPN, a tool still logged in, or a stale session. Turn off VPNs, stop all tools, log in on your usual device and complete the check once.',
 [('Turn off the VPN', 'Shared or masked networks are a common reason.'),
  ('Stop all tools', 'Any app acting on the account keeps the flag alive.'),
  ('Use your usual device', 'A known device passes more easily.')],
 [S('Common reasons', ul(['VPNs, proxies and public Wi-Fi.', 'Third-party tools still connected to the account.', 'Many rapid actions, such as follows or comments.', 'Multiple people logging in from different places.'])),
  S('What to try', ol(['Disconnect from the VPN and use your normal connection.', 'Remove any connected tool and extension.', 'Log in on your usual phone and complete the check once.', 'If it loops, take a screen recording and send it to us.']),
    'Repeatedly tapping through can add more checks. Try calmly and leave the account alone for a while if it does not pass.')],
 [('Does it mean the account is banned?', 'No. It is a security check, not a ban.'),
  ('Can I wait it out?', 'Sometimes it passes after a break from the account. If it persists, change the network and device.'),
  ('Are captcha solving tools allowed?', 'No. Do not use them. They can make things worse.')],
 ['People who cannot pass the human check.', 'Teams who share a login.', 'Owners who use a VPN.'])

page('instagram-selfie-with-glasses-or-head-covering', F, 'Instagram Selfie Verification With Glasses or Head Covering',
 'Instagram verification asks for a clear face and you wear glasses or a head covering? What usually works and how to frame the video so it is readable.',
 'Instagram selfie when you wear glasses or a head covering?', 'Selfie with glasses or head covering',
 'The check needs to see your face clearly. Glasses and head coverings are common, and there are ways to frame it.',
 'The selfie check needs your whole face visible. If you wear glasses, glare can hide your eyes, so tilt the phone slightly or remove them for the video. If you wear a head covering for religious or medical reasons, keep your face fully visible from forehead to chin, and add a short note in the request if it allows one.',
 [('Reduce the glare', 'Move away from lamps that reflect on the lens.'),
  ('Full face in view', 'Forehead to chin, with both ears optional.'),
  ('Add a note if you can', 'One short line explaining that you wear it every day.')],
 [S('What the check looks for', ul(['A clear view of the eyes, nose and mouth.', 'Even light across the face.', 'A match with the face on the ID, if one is requested.', 'A natural, unedited video.']),
    'People wear glasses and head coverings in their own ID photos too, so reviewers see them often.'),
  S('Recording tips', ol(['Sit facing the light with no strong lamp behind you.', 'Wear what you wear in your ID photo, unless it hides the face.', 'Tilt the glasses slightly if they glare, or remove them if the video fails.', 'Move slowly through the on-screen steps.']))],
 [('Do I have to remove my glasses?', 'Not always. If the video fails because of glare, try without them.'),
  ('Is there a special route for head coverings?', 'There is no separate route. A clear face is the main need.'),
  ('Can Unbanz speak to Instagram on my behalf?', 'We prepare what you send. Instagram makes the decision.')],
 ['People who wear glasses and fail the check.', 'People who wear a religious or medical head covering.', 'Anyone whose selfie is rejected for the face being unclear.'])

page('instagram-selfie-verification-poor-light-or-camera', F, 'Instagram Selfie Check With a Poor Camera or Low Light',
 'Your phone camera is weak or your room is dark and Instagram selfie checks fail? Practical ways to record a readable video without special equipment.',
 'Instagram selfie fails in low light or on a weak camera?', 'Selfie in poor light or camera',
 'You do not need a new phone. Most failures are about light and steadiness.',
 'Instagram selfie checks fail on dark, grainy or shaky video. You can improve it without new equipment: sit near a window in daylight, lean the phone against something steady, clean the lens, and keep still except for the movements the screen asks for. If the front camera is poor, ask a family member to lend a better phone.',
 [('Use daylight', 'A window gives the best light on your face.'),
  ('Steady the phone', 'Rest it on a stack of books at eye level.'),
  ('Clean the lens', 'A smudged front camera ruins video.')],
 [S('Why weak cameras fail', ul(['Grain and noise in dim rooms.', 'Shaky hands changing the frame.', 'Auto exposure making the face too dark against a bright background.', 'Low storage or a slow phone dropping frames.']),
    'Clear some storage and close other apps before starting.'),
  S('Setup that helps', ol(['Face a window, with no lamp or window behind you.', 'Wipe the camera with a soft cloth.', 'Lean the phone against a steady object at eye level.', 'Record in one take, and wait for the prompt before each movement.']),
    'If you borrow a device, log in on it only to take the selfie where the flow allows, and do not save your login there.')],
 [('Is a second device allowed?', 'Only if the flow lets you continue on it. Do not share your password with others.'),
  ('How good does the video have to be?', 'Clear enough to see your face. It does not need to be high definition.'),
  ('What if it fails again?', 'Tell us the message you see. We can help work out what the request needs.')],
 ['People with older phones.', 'People in dim rooms or at night.', 'Anyone whose video keeps failing to process.'])

page('instagram-id-request-business-account-owner', F, 'Instagram ID Request on a Business Account',
 'Instagram asked the owner of a business account for ID and you are not sure whose to send? How to handle owner ID, company details and team access.',
 'Instagram asked for ID on a business account?', 'ID request on a business account',
 'A business account still has a person behind it, and the request is about that person. Here is how to handle it.',
 'On a business account, the ID request is usually about the person who controls the account, not the company. The account owner sends their own document, and a staff member should not send the director’s ID. If the request also asks for business details, send what is shown on the request screen.',
 [('The owner sends it', 'Not a colleague, and not an agency.'),
  ('Business papers if asked', 'Only the documents the screen names.'),
  ('Keep admin roles clean', 'Know who has access before you start.')],
 [S('Why it is asked', ul(['The account was flagged for unusual login activity.', 'The account was reported for impersonation or misleading claims.', 'A hacker may have taken control and the owner must be verified.', 'The business connected a verified Page or ad account.'])),
  S('How to handle it', ol(['Decide who the account owner is and have that person do the request.', 'Use the official screen only and send the document it lists.', 'If it asks for company details, use the registration paperwork that matches the name on the account.', 'Share the screens with us, but never send the ID in a message.']),
    'Agencies managing client accounts should have the client submit their own ID.')],
 [('Can a manager send their own ID?', 'No. It needs to be the person who owns or controls the account.'),
  ('What if the owner is abroad?', 'The owner can still complete it from where they are. A different phone location can be mentioned in the notes.'),
  ('Should the agency handle it?', 'The client should, since the check is about identity.')],
 ['Small business owners.', 'Agencies and managers working for clients.', 'Founders with brand accounts.'])

page('instagram-verification-stuck-on-reviewing', F, 'Instagram Verification Stuck on Reviewing',
 'Your Instagram ID or selfie is stuck on reviewing for a long time? What the status means, how to check it safely and when to act instead of waiting.',
 'Instagram verification stuck on reviewing?', 'Verification stuck on reviewing',
 'A review with no outcome is frustrating. Here is how to tell waiting from a stalled submission.',
 'A status of reviewing means the submission was received, but it does not say how long a decision takes, and there is no public timer. Check that you got a confirmation, check your email and spam, and avoid sending it again. If the status never changes and nothing arrives, ask us about other routes.',
 [('Confirm it was received', 'Look for a confirmation screen or email.'),
  ('Do not resubmit', 'Duplicates can restart the queue.'),
  ('Check all inboxes', 'The answer may have gone to an old address.')],
 [S('What may be happening', ul(['The request is simply queued.', 'The submission was incomplete, and no reply is coming.', 'The reply went to a different email.', 'The account status changed with no notification.']),
    'Instagram does not publish review times.'),
  S('What to do', ol(['Log in and screenshot the current status and date.', 'Search every inbox for messages about the account.', 'Wait without resubmitting, and check at intervals instead of constantly.', 'If nothing changes after a long wait, contact us with the screenshots.']))],
 [('Does reviewing mean progress?', 'It means received. It does not predict the outcome.'),
  ('Can Unbanz speed it up?', 'No. We cannot jump the queue and nobody outside can.'),
  ('When is it worth trying another route?', 'When the status has not changed for a long time and nothing else is arriving.')],
 ['People who submitted and heard nothing.', 'Owners of business accounts waiting on a decision.', 'Anyone unsure whether the upload went through.'])
